    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "The Dalakas criteria for the diagnosis of stiff person syndrome: Stiffness in the axial muscles, especially in the abdominal and thoracolumbar paraspinal muscles leading to a fixed deformity typically hyperlordosis; Superimposed painful spasms triggered by emotional stress, tactile stimuli, sudden noises; Electromyography confirmation of continuous motor unit activity simultaneously occurring in both agonist and antagonist muscles; Absence of other neurologic or cognitive disease causing the stiffness/rigidity; Positive serology for GAD65 (or amphiphysin) autoantibodies by immunocytochemistry, western blot or radioimmunoassay; Response to diazepam. These criteria were all fulfilled by this patient.",
      "quote": "The Dalakas criteria for the diagnosis of stiff person syndrome ... These criteria were all fulfilled by this patient.",
